WEBVTT

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:09.570
<b>I want to be connected
A</b>

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:09.570
<b>I want to be connected
A</b>

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.240
<i>Nii-san gave up everything for me.</i>

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:17.740
<i>So I'm going to give up what's 
most precious to me, too.</i>

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.250
<b>"Kaisou"</b>

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.250
<b>O Flashback</b>

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.250
<b>X Seaweed</b>

00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:30.760
Why are you throwing it away?

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.460
Do you hate it now?

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:35.330
No.

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:38.500
But to survive, I have to throw it away.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.020
Was that the same for me, too?

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:44.710
I'm not connected to anyone.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:49.770
People realize they were connected 
when they no longer are.

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:53.410
I have to protect the connections I have.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:55.780
So I'm giving up soccer.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:05.750
Take it.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:09.650
Some dreams come true because 
you're disconnected.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:16.420
<i>Of course he wouldn't remember.</i>

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:20.440
I guess this is the last 
time I see this place.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:21.730
Nii-san.

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:22.810
Is everything okay?

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:23.840
What's going on?

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:24.950
Who knows?

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:29.190
But there's a good chance they've sniffed 
out what happened four years ago.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.780
You'd better not still be 
thinking that it's your fault.

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:36.700
Not really.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:39.110
Don't forget, though.

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:43.700
Just as you need me, I need you.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:46.080
Come with me, Toi.

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:47.530
Nii-san...

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:51.890
What's wrong?

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:54.090
Give me just a little time.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.800
No, I'm going with you.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.290
I've made up my mind about that.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:02.900
But there are a couple of people 
I want to make sure are okay.

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:09.100
I haven't seen you make that face in a while.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.880
Fine, fine.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.110
I'll be waiting.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:14.480
But only for one day.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:17.020
Yeah.

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:33.460
<i>Once the background blends together,
there's an invisible street corner</i>

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:38.050
<i>There we are, crying out with fading voices</i>

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:42.720
<i>Go forth with the tearing pain</i>

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:47.350
<i>As though you'd just crawled
away from the worst night ever</i>

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:51.520
<i>You're always alone</i>

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:56.160
<i>Your heart is shouting a sound of desire</i>

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:01.780
<i>If we can ever talk again,
if we can ever connect</i>

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:05.520
<i>I'd be overwhelmed</i>

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.660
<i>You grow more and more distant</i>

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:11.370
<i>I chase after you</i>

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:19.130
<i>To tell you my brand new feelings for you</i>

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.860
<i>I run like mad</i>

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:27.010
<i>Present, past and future</i>

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:29.100
<i>I want to be connected with you</i>

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:32.610
<i>By our feelings, by the depths of our souls</i>

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:50.900
Damn it, Kazuki! That bastard!

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.460
Why do I have to take all the flack?

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:57.960
Who's more important, me or him?

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:01.970
Huh?

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.670
Out of balls already?

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:06.120
Damn it, everything sucks.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:09.710
When everything sucks, 
just throw it all away.

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:12.010
You only live once.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:15.690
You don't get extra lives.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:24.130
Holy...

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.490
See?

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.240
Is there something on my face?

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:31.910
No, nothing.

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:34.750
Oh, here. Thanks.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:38.260
Helping people sure does pay off.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:40.810
Tch.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:45.410
The leader of a fraud ring that 
was working out of the Tama region...

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:46.890
Why do we have to deal with it?

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:49.410
The suspect lives in this town.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:51.270
So?

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:56.020
<b>Shikotama Fraud Incident in Tama, Tokyo
 April to June, 2019</b>

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:55.430
Apparently, he's wanted in connection
to a fatal shooting four years ago.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:59.230
If we capture him, we can easily 
make him a kappa zombie.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:05.150
Look at this half-baked doll, 
so eager to please those people.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:11.350
Do you honestly think this'll change my mind?

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:19.790
This is only half-baked.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:28.330
A-All clear.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:35.060
<b>Pedestrians have 
the right of way</b>

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:35.060
<b>Karaokeya</b>

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.060
Man, I owe you.

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:36.830
Do you know this place well?

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:41.690
<b>Umeya</b>

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:41.690
I used to hang out here with Kazu—
my friend—ever since I was little.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:44.820
Everything changes before you know it.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.450
The town, the people...

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:47.950
<b>Enjoy the day with song and dance</b>

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:49.820
Did you do something bad?

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:55.060
Hey, Specs, how old are you?

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:55.700
Huh?

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:57.590
I'm fourteen. Why?

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.690
You're pretty small for fourteen.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:03.960
<b>Sarafuku</b>

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:03.960
<b>Japan's Cucumbers</b>

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:03.960
<b>Sarafuku's Cucumbers</b>

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:01.140
That's none of your business!

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:02.950
My bad.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:07.300
I happen to have a brother 
that's about your age.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.210
I know.

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:10.910
I don't know if it's because I haven't 
kept up with him for a while,

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:13.470
but he's gotten so grown-up. 
He's not cute anymore.

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:16.390
I'm leaving town with him.

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:19.730
I can't let myself get caught right now.

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:23.530
Hey...

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:26.990
If it's all right with you, I'd like to help.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:27.910
Huh?

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:30.990
<b>Union</b>

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:30.990
Grow up already.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.410
But aren't you pissed off, too?

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:38.500
We could have granted your wish by now.

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.930
I'm disappointed in Enta.

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:44.930
He lied to us and betrayed us.

00:06:44.930 --> 00:06:47.300
I'm sure he has his reasons.

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:49.430
What reasons?

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:50.630
Well...

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:52.330
That's not for me to say.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:54.410
What the hell?

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:56.000
So you two are keeping a secret?

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.500
Why are you siding with Enta?

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:00.890
No, that's not what I'm doing.

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:01.990
Forget it.

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:03.150
I'm going to find the dishes.

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:04.650
Hey!

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:11.660
<b>Kappa
Plaza</b>

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:10.590
Shit. I'm not good at handling
 these situations...

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:23.670
<b>Sicko Top Man of Shikotama in Hiding?</b>

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:23.670
<b>Asakusa</b>

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:23.670
<b><i></i></b>I have something important to tell the prince today, dish. I never would have thought <i>they</i> were behind it, dish... But to me, those two don't seem like bad people.

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:13.920
<i>Now for the next story, dish.</i>

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:16.810
<i>The police force has made 
an emergency deployment</i>

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:20.690
<i>in response to the possibility 
that Kuji Chikai, 25,</i>

00:07:20.690 --> 00:07:26.830
<i>wanted leader of nefarious fraud 
ring Shikotama, is hiding out in Asakusa.</i>

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:27.420
<b>Sicko Top Man of Shikotama in Hiding?</b>

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.420
<b>Asakusa</b>

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.420
<b>Sicko Top Man of Shikotama in Hiding?</b>

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.420
<b><i></i></b>I have something important to tell the prince today, dish. I never would have thought <i>they</i> were behind it, dish... But to me, those two don't seem like bad people.

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.420
<i>Freeze! Freeze!</i>

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:31.940
I'm out of time.

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:36.930
<b>Hanayashiki</b>

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:41.480
I haven't been to Hanayashiki in ages.

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:48.730
He used to follow me around,
all like, "Nii-chan, Nii-chan..."

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:51.700
Before I knew it, he's a different person.

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:57.050
He's trying to choose between me
 and his buddies right now.

00:07:58.180 --> 00:07:59.170
Buddies?

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:01.850
I mean, I can't blame him.

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:06.000
I made him give up something 
precious to him, after all.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.000
<b>"Kaisou"</b>

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.000
<b>O Flashback</b>

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.000
<b>X Seaweed</b>

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:12.010
That's the end of it.

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:14.860
Forget about the gun.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:16.140
Got it?

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.070
Yeah.

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:19.140
I'll catch up with you later.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:20.340
Sure.

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:33.220
You gave up everything for me.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:36.660
So I'm going to give up what's 
most precious to me, too.

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:41.870
He gave up soccer.

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:49.590
He used to say he wanted to become 
a soccer player when he grew up.

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:53.050
No...

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:54.910
...way...

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:57.750
This miçanga...

00:09:00.710 --> 00:09:03.300
He said he gave the miçanga away, too.

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:04.060
To who?!

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.720
Who did he give it to?!

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:07.860
I wouldn't know.

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:14.070
I'm sure he wanted someone to remember 
how much soccer meant to him.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:17.820
He's too earnest, really.

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:23.020
He'd put himself in danger or 
get his hands dirty for my sake.

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:25.340
Even though it's not like I asked him to.

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:28.830
Me, too.

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:32.840
I would have done anything for Kazuki.

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:37.790
No matter how much you do for someone, 
if it bears no fruit, it's not worth anything.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:40.850
That depends on how you look at it yourself.

00:09:41.410 --> 00:09:44.930
Just do whatever will make 
things easiest for you, then.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.210
That's...

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:49.350
<b>Roller Coaster</b>

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:04.750
Taito Ward Bulletin Board

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:00.850
I guess I'm out of time.

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:02.290
You are.

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:04.750
Hurry up, take your brother, and leave.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:09.240
Chikai...

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:10.740
Who the heck is that?

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:11.630
Oh, shit.

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:15.130
I'm going to avenge my bro!

00:10:27.490 --> 00:10:29.250
No, I, uh...

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:32.820
H-Hey!

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:33.650
Yo, kid.

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:35.620
Are you with Chikai?

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:36.650
N-No, I'm not.

00:10:36.650 --> 00:10:38.640
Don't play dumb with me!

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:41.660
Over here, policeman!

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:43.330
<i>We're</i> the police.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:45.410
This happens all the time.

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:47.320
What are you doing to that child?

00:10:47.320 --> 00:10:49.580
You're violating the Firearms
and Swords Control Act, you know.

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:54.480
I've lived my life until now to kill Chikai.

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:54.220
Shit, shit, shit!

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:55.510
Chikai...

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:59.230
Are you talking about the 
wanted fugitive, Kuji Chikai?

00:10:59.230 --> 00:11:01.550
I'm not letting you popos have him!

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:05.060
Let him take responsibility 
for taking out my bro!

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:06.710
This guy's so stuffy.

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:08.100
Kuji's gotten away already.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.810
Quit babbling!

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:18.720
Damn it...

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:20.410
Stay out of our way.

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:23.820
We're in the middle of 
the street, but oh well.

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:27.080
Do you think you can threaten me with that?

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:29.580
We'll open this door for you.

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:33.330
Desire or love?

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:34.080
<b>Fire</b>

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:57.660
What do we do with this?

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:00.020
He's valuable kappa zombie material.

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:01.490
What was that gunshot?

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:03.490
There's a man down.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:06.330
Oh dear, we got caught.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:07.490
He's dead.

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:09.410
Did you two shoot him?

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:11.500
This isn't going to pass as self-defense.

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:15.420
Hey, why don't you two say something?

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:17.500
It was Kuji the fugitive who shot him.

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:19.690
What are you talking about?

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:23.510
Kuji made enemies from the 
incident four years ago.

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:24.850
Exactly.

00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:26.590
It's Kuji's fault.

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:28.140
But there's no proof of that anywhere...

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:34.930
Who shot this man?

00:12:34.930 --> 00:12:36.410
Kuji the fugitive.

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:37.520
Without a doubt.

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:47.030
<b>Kaminari Gorogoro Kaikan</b>

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:47.570
I've been watching them 
for the past few days.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:52.540
I'm certain that these two people 
have captured Dark Keppi-sama, dish.

00:12:51.430 --> 00:12:52.540
<b>Yakisoba</b>

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:53.790
<b>Fire</b>

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:54.490
Reo and Mabu...

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.920
I never thought they'd still be alive, kero.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:01.550
And this is our secret anti-otter weapon, dish!

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:04.550
<b>Secret Anti-Otter Weapon</b>

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:04.550
What's this?

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:10.470
It freezes the target solid at the flick 
of a switch, so we can catch them alive, dish.

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:11.560
I see.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:14.790
Then let's first determine 
their current location, kero.

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:17.810
<b>Kappa Ken</b>

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:17.810
<b>Sara
Pepper</b>

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:19.310
Can't fight on an empty stomach.

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:20.690
Pepper...

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:22.320
<b>Kappa Ken</b>

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:22.320
<b>Sara
Pepper</b>

00:13:32.050 --> 00:13:33.300
Prince!

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:41.350
Out cold...

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:43.300
Oh no, dish!

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:45.880
The live broadcast is coming up, dish.

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:48.590
I can't be late!

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:50.460
You're so horrible!

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:51.580
I thought I was dead!

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:54.630
The bad ones are the ones 
who survive in this world.

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:58.290
Softies like you should
be careful, Specs.

00:13:58.290 --> 00:13:59.600
You think <i>you</i> have the right to say that?

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:04.740
Well, now that you're still alive, you should
 go make up with your buddies.

00:14:05.230 --> 00:14:07.010
No, I don't really...

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:10.440
I gotta go.

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:12.020
Share those with your buddies.

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:16.530
Hey, Masa.

00:14:16.530 --> 00:14:18.460
I'm taking a boat there now.

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:21.380
Toi's coming, too, of course.

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:26.380
<i>Jinnai?</i>

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:27.740
<i>About Yasaka...</i>

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:29.440
Why didn't you say anything?

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:30.090
<i>Huh?</i>

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:33.140
About the miçanga you gave Kazuki!

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:35.810
<i>He remembered?</i>

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:38.890
No, I don't think he realizes.

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:40.090
I see.

00:14:40.950 --> 00:14:42.070
Of course.

00:14:42.070 --> 00:14:43.900
<i>Why didn't you tell Kazuki?</i>

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:46.750
He doesn't remember anything.

00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:49.150
There's no reason to tell him now.

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:53.060
<i>You two go on as the golden duo.</i>

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:55.160
Are you happy with that?

00:14:56.780 --> 00:14:58.630
I'm going to live for my brother.

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:00.910
Bye.

